ufs-qcom (soc-repo fork): build against the 6.18 UFS core

The fork stays (not upstream ufs-qcom): the vendor DT keeps the 6.12 UFS nodes, and the vendor
PHY driver phy-qcom-ufs-qmp-v4-yupik takes its per-UFS-vendor tables and lane/hibern8 calls
from ufs_qcom_phy_*() calls that only this host driver makes (see PORT-STATUS.md).

- enum ufs_trace_str_t moved from <ufs/ufs.h> to drivers/ufs/core/ufs_trace_types.h.
- ufshcd_dme_rmw() is exported by the 6.18 core; the static copy in ufs-qcom.h goes.
- the MCQ resource table (enum ufshcd_res, struct ufshcd_res_info, hba->res[]) left struct
  ufs_hba: same table, kept in struct ufs_qcom_host. MCQ is UFSHCI 4.0 and unused on the
  SM7325 controller; this only keeps the code building.
- msi_lock_descs()/msi_unlock_descs() -> __msi_lock_descs()/__msi_unlock_descs() (the 6.18
  msi_descs_lock guard's primitives).
- ufs_stats.last_intr_status/_ts are gone: dropped from the error dump.
- UFS_DEVICE_QUIRK_DELAY_AFTER_LPM is gone: the 6.18 core waits hba->vcc_off_delay_us after
  every VCC-off (2 ms default); set to 5000, the quirk's 5 ms, which applied to the Samsung
  part of this phone.
- pwr_change_notify() lost dev_max_params: the PRE_CHANGE negotiation moved to the new
  .negotiate_pwr_mode op (same ufs_qcom_get_pwr_dev_param() call).
- ufs_hba_variant_ops.program_key is gone: with SCSI_UFS_CRYPTO_QTI (lahaina config) the host
  sets UFSHCD_QUIRK_CUSTOM_CRYPTO_PROFILE and ufshcd-crypto-qti programs the keyslots, so the
  core never called it on 6.12 either.

